# Task 05 — NTLM / NTHash

I first inspected the file:

```bash
cat ntlm.txt
```

I also used:

```bash
python3 hash-id.py
```

Initially, I tried MD5 formats:

```bash
john --format=md5 --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt ntlm.txt
```

and:

```bash
john --format=raw-MD5 --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt ntlm.txt
```

### Mistake

The hash was an NTLM/NTHash type, not an MD5 hash.

So using an MD5 format was a **hash-format identification mistake**.

I then searched John's formats and used:

```bash
john --format=NT --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt ntlm.txt
```

### Lesson

Do not choose the John format just because the hash looks like another hexadecimal hash.

First identify the hash type, then choose the corresponding John format.

