# Final Learning

The biggest thing I learned from this room was not just individual commands.

It was understanding the pattern:

```text
Different password-protected source
              ↓
     Convert/prepare data
              ↓
      John-readable input
              ↓
       Choose attack mode
              ↓
         Crack password
```

John's syntax becomes much easier once I know:

```text
What is my input?
What format is it?
Does it need conversion?
Which John mode am I using?
Where is my wordlist?
```

That is the core workflow I want to remember from this room.
